WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.410
- A couple of years ago,

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:05.430
I applied to the strategy
consulting firm, McKinsey.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.940
And I got in.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.770
In this video, I'm going to show you

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.920
the real CV that I used
to apply to McKinsey,

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.700
and that landed me the job.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.290
This is no click-bait, guys.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.240
I'm showing you the real thing,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.940
the actual document that I handed in

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.890
when I submitted my application.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.680
To those of you who don't know me yet,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.070
welcome to my channel, Firm Learning.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.100
My name is Heinrich, and I'm
a former McKinsey consultant.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.250
I worked with the firm for
about six years in the end,

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.760
serving as a project lead.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.520
About a year ago, I
transitioned from McKinsey

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.620
into a C-level role at
a German retail company.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.360
And I started this YouTube
channel, Firm Learning,

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.407
to talk about my experiences,

00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:47.950
and my tips and tricks,

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.470
what you can do to become successful

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.310
in the first years of your career.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:55.240
So without further ado,
let's jump into the CV.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.480
I just have two introductory remarks.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.610
The first is that I blacked out

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.690
a couple of personal information,

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:03.450
but all the rest, everything else,

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.860
this is really the document that I used.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.693
The second is that,

00:01:06.693 --> 00:01:10.130
because I applied to the
German office at that time,

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.680
my CV is in German.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.120
And I did not want to now
tamper with the document.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.100
So I'm showing you the
actual version, in German.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.680
But of course, the whole video
is going to be in English,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.590
and I'm going to explain you in detail

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.090
all the individual sections.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.210
So trust you're going to get lots of value

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.860
out of this video, even if
you do not speak German.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.010
This is it, guys.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:32.600
This is the real CV that I
used to apply to McKinsey,

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.930
and I got in.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.640
Let's now first go over
the overall structure,

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.460
and then we go over each
of the positions in detail.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.967
So what you see is that here,

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.800
above, I have this
header segment of the CV.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.740
Then I have a segment called 'Ausbildung',

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.030
this means education.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.810
So these are all my university
degrees and things like that.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.830
Then 'Arbeitserfahrung',
this means work experience.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.180
Then 'Extracurriculare Aktivitäten',

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.620
this means extracurricular activities.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.160
Then 'Stipendien', this
means scholarships.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.490
And qualifications.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:06.100
Let's now go over each of
these segments in detail.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.330
And what I wanna say in the beginning is

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.410
that probably today,

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:13.560
I would make some of the
things a bit differently.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.040
I wouldn't phrase those
things exactly like this.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.490
I might do some changes to the structure,

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.950
but at that time, I
just didn't know better.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.440
But let's start with the header,

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.650
here it's just pretty basic.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.390
You see my name, you see my date of birth.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:30.080
You see where I was born, and
then here my postal address,

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.330
as well as a telephone
number and an email.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.210
Next, let's talk about
the education section.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.410
So let's start at the bottom,

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:38.450
this is ordered anti-chronologically,

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.377
so the oldest position is here below.

00:02:40.377 --> 00:02:42.284
And this was my high school degree,

00:02:42.284 --> 00:02:45.040
Gymnasium Johanneum, this was
the name of my high school.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.560
And what you see here
are my focus courses.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.480
So in Germany, you can
choose a couple of subjects

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.690
that you really focus on,

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:55.110
I chose biology and social sciences.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.710
And what I always included,
I just blacked it out,

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.840
just the GPA, the grade that I got.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.340
Next is Universita
Commerciale Luigi Bocconi.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.340
This is my exchange semester,
so I stayed one semester

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.240
at the University Bocconi,
which is, at least in Europe,

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.700
quite well-known business
school in Milan, in Italy.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.240
Then my main university degree,

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.110
this was the university in Munich,

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.960
Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.040
And actually, what I
did was a double degree.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:23.070
So I studied in two
independent bachelor programs

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.650
at the time, I studied
business administration,

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:26.990
that was the first one.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.250
And then philosophy.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.351
And as philosophy I had a minor in first

00:03:30.351 --> 00:03:31.240
(chuckling) history of arts,

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.230
and later economics.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.750
And again, I included here the grades.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:34.680
And when I applied,

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.780
I was in the fifth semester
of my bachelor studies,

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.970
so I didn't complete these degrees yet,

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.560
but of course I had a GPA.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.650
And then finally, a honors
degree in technology management,

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.540
at the Center for Digital
Technology and Management,

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.760
that was an honors degree,

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:51.340
an additional degree that you
were able to do in Munich,

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.470
which was focused on, as the name says,

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:54.580
technology and management.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.210
And here again, I believe it
was still ongoing at that time,

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.890
so I included the current GPA.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.700
So let's move to the next section,

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.530
and this is the section
on the work experience.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.930
So what was the practical
experience that I had

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.480
when I applied to McKinsey, at the time?

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.840
And again, let's start
anti-chronologically.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.240
Here the first one,
this was an internship,

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:16.770
internship is called
'Praktikum' in Germany.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.290
And this was at Miele.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.070
So Miele is, at least in Germany,

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.280
a pretty well-known company

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.340
that mainly is well-known
for kitchen appliances.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.870
And this was an internship
I did between my high school

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.950
and the start of the university studies.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.510
So I was there for about one month,

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:34.330
working in the customer
service department.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.400
And I was working on a training platform,

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.950
an e-learning platform,

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.670
that they were currently putting together

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.670
to train all their technicians
all around the world.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:46.010
Then after the first semester
of my business degree,

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.520
I did an internship at
Harry Rosen in Toronto.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.070
Harry Rosen is a large Canadian menswear

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.900
premium fashion retailer.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.360
And I rotated between
different departments,

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.120
I was at the point of sale,

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.700
but probably mainly supporting
the merchandise team,

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.730
among other teams.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.720
Then both during high school

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.750
up to my first semesters in university,

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.680
I worked in my family business,

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.840
and I collected mainly
experiences in the buying team,

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:13.280
but also in the sales team.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:15.960
We are a medium-sized company in Germany,

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.890
and of course, working
in the family business

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:20.000
is always a bit of a different experience

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.660
than working in any other business.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.050
But still, for me, this was
very practical work experience

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.150
that I collected at the time.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.550
Next, I completed an
internship at Accenture.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:31.890
Accenture is a very
large IT consulting firm,

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.840
and now this was my first
very significant internship

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.170
that also went on for a couple of months.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.820
And what I did here is, I
supported an SAP implementation

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.830
in a large technical client.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.670
So I was part of the consulting team,

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.400
working on-site with the client.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.930
And now this was really the
first time I experienced

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:53.390
what it was like to work in a
large international company,

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:55.210
both on the consulting side of things,

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.930
but then also at the client.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.650
And this internship worked pretty well,

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.950
because then after the
internship finished,

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:02.830
I worked as a working student.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:04.840
I worked just as a part-time job,

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.700
during my university
studies, at that client.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.610
So all in all, this was almost half a year

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.890
of work experience, in parallel
to my university studies,

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.250
that I collected at Accenture.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.350
Then later, I worked
with a technical company,

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:20.150
Telefonica, and this now
wasn't really an internship,

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.890
this was rather project work.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:24.820
So this was coming out
of a university class,

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:27.050
where we worked together with Telefonica.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:29.800
And then Telefonica
asked us to support them,

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:32.900
in their business development
team on a project work,

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.540
and we developed a business plan.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.580
A business plan for a new product

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.680
they were thinking about launching.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.350
And it was not only the business plan,

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:43.220
but we were working in an
interdisciplinary student team,

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.170
and we also had iOS developers.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.360
We had actually computer science students,

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.205
who then built the first prototype,

00:06:49.205 --> 00:06:51.960
(chuckling) that was really
running on our iPhones in iOS!

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:55.420
To really bring a first
vision of that product, live,

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:56.380
into our phones.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:58.730
And then finally, I took on a regular job

00:06:58.730 --> 00:06:59.680
with a professor,

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:02.810
with Professor Picot at
his university institute.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.250
And I supported him in his research.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.590
So this now was a real academic job,

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.840
I was supporting him with his papers,

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.830
with the research, in a research team.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.640
So this was now for me getting to know

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:15.710
the academia side of things,

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.220
what all of this is like.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:21.030
So let's now move to the
extracurricular side of things.

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:22.780
And again, let's start with the older one.

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:24.140
This was something I was doing

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:25.920
still in parallel to my high school.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.123
And I was invited by Siemens, actually,

00:07:28.123 --> 00:07:30.400
I got a scholarship from Siemens

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.350
to start university studies

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:34.810
in parallel to my high school studies.

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:36.660
So in the end of my high school time,

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.607
I started at a local 'Fachhochschule',

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:42.270
which is a university of applied sciences,

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.810
to take on some first business exams.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.640
So this for me was a great opportunity

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.760
to already get to know what it's like

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:51.867
to study at university,
during my high school time.

00:07:51.867 --> 00:07:55.110
And then a second large
extracurricular activity is,

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.340
that I had at the time,

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:58.560
that I worked in a youth organization,

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.360
of a large political party in Germany.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.820
And I was the leader of the local chapter

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:05.650
of that youth organization.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:06.830
So I blacked that out,

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:09.800
because I do not want to
talk about my political views

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.300
here in public, on YouTube.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.130
But it was one of the very
large political parties

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:14.963
in Germany.

00:08:14.963 --> 00:08:16.980
And this was actually
one of the things I did

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.940
that really gave me lots of input,

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:20.440
lots of things to talk about

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:22.120
in the personal impact interview,

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.710
in the interview where you are asked

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.860
to talk about your leadership experiences,

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:28.630
where you are asked to talk
about how you led teams,

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:30.250
how you worked together with teams.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.520
Because as you can imagine,

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:34.580
this was also during
the election year, 2009.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.900
Where we had lots of elections
going on at that year,

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:39.200
so there was really lots
of things to organize.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.860
And this was really lots of
material that I could draw from.

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:44.220
Next is the scholarships section.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.870
So at the time, when I applied,

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.920
I had the Cusanuswerk Scholarship,

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.250
which is one of the
large public scholarships

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.830
that you can collect in Germany.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.240
And then Max-Weber Programm Scholarship,

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.790
which is conducted by
the 'Studienstiftung',

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:00.060
which is the German
national merit foundation,

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.070
I believe this is what the translation is.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.550
So this is specific thing in Bavaria,

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:06.180
where you can then get it.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:09.500
And these scholarships pretty
much provide funding to you,

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:10.870
for your university degrees.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:13.120
But in Germany, they're
also well-regarded,

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:15.780
because the selection
process is quite complex,

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.710
with an assessment center
and things like that.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:19.980
Which is why consulting
firms like McKinsey

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:21.960
usually tend to very much like this.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.390
And then the Siemens scholarship

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.450
that I already talked about,

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.830
which enabled me to fund my studies

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.100
in parallel to my high school.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.130
And then a section about
other qualifications,

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:32.360
and here I included my language skills.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:33.650
This is of course English,

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.730
and I already did a
TOEFL test at the time,

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.650
because when I applied to McKinsey,

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:41.250
I already completed my TOEFL
for the Master applications

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.100
that I had out there.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.490
And in the end, you maybe already know,

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:44.710
that then I ended up doing

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.660
a Master of Accounting and Finance,

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:49.030
at the London School
of Economics in London.

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:50.330
So the time sequence was

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:52.780
that I completed my
internship during my bachelor,

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.600
then I already received an
offer to join McKinsey later.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:58.550
But then I first did this
one-year Master in London,

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.820
and then I joined
McKinsey after the Master.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:02.690
So this is why I already
had the TOEFL test.

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:05.530
Then I spoke Italian, also
because I studied in Milan,

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:07.210
as I told you, for an exchange semester.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.607
And then I had Latinum in high school.

00:10:08.607 --> 00:10:11.040
And then I also included my GMAT score,

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.240
which, again, I already did

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.340
because I did these Master applications.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.360
And then I included the computer skills

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.330
that I had at the time.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:20.070
So that's it, guys, this was my CV.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:22.170
This was the real document,

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:25.180
the real thing that I used at that time

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.730
when I applied to MBB firms like McKinsey.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.600
And again, due to this application,

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.730
